# Arduino Auto Night Light (Smooth Fade + LDR)

A small Arduino project that turns a light on automatically when the room is dark and applies a smooth “breathing” fade effect. Includes an optional push button to force the light ON or return to AUTO mode.

## Demo behavior
- Bright room → LED OFF
- Dark room → LED breathes (smooth fade in/out)
- Optional button → toggles FORCE ON / AUTO

## Parts
- Arduino Uno / Nano (or compatible)
- 1× LED (any color)  
- 1× 220Ω resistor (for LED)
- 1× LDR (photoresistor)
- 1× 10kΩ resistor (for LDR voltage divider)
- (Optional) 1× push button + jumper wires

## Wiring
### LED (PWM)
- Arduino D9 → 220Ω resistor → LED anode (+)
- LED cathode (-) → GND

### LDR voltage divider to A0
- 5V → LDR → node → 10kΩ → GND
- node → A0

### Optional button (uses internal pull-up)
- One side of button → D2
- Other side of button → GND

## How to run
1. Open `src/auto_night_light.ino` in Arduino IDE.
2. Select your board + COM port.
3. Upload.
4. Cover the LDR to simulate darkness.

## Tuning
- `DARK_THRESHOLD` controls when the LED turns on.
- `FADE_STEP` and `FADE_DELAY_MS` control breathing speed.
- Use Serial Monitor to inspect the raw LDR readings.

